    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`, and the only existing test passes. That test just checks that `LABELS` is lower-case, so it doesn't exercise the new function. I tried to check the request with a fake client, but the environment blocked running inline Python. No live API call has been made either.\n\nWhat the function does:\n- **One request:** it makes a single `client.messages.create` call to `MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with `max_tokens=5` and `temperature=0`.\n- **Prompts:** the system prompt tells the model to answer with exactly one word from `bug, feature, question` and nothing else. The ticket text is sent as the user message.\n- **Reading the reply:** it joins the text blocks in the response, then strips and lower-cases the result. If that isn't one of `LABELS`, it returns `\"question\"`. This also covers replies with no text, such as a refusal.\n\nSonnet 4.6 accepts `temperature=0`. Newer models (Sonnet 5, the Opus 4.7+ family, Fable 5) return a 400 error for any sampling parameter. If `MODEL` is ever changed to one of those, the request will fail and the temperature setting will have to be removed. No dependencies were added."
